        {
          "title": "Body scans, ref cams and football AI: Inside the World Cup’s new era",
          "summary": "The New York Times examines how AI is shaping the 2026 World Cup, from body-scanning analytics and AI-assisted refereeing to automated match-tracking systems. The piece discusses pilots underway, potential benefits in decision accuracy and broadcast experience, and the challenges around transparency, bias, and data privacy for players and officials.",
          "source": "https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/7087240/2026/03/06/ai-world-cup-technology-ref-camera-body-scans/",
          "signature": "dafdac8bfa0a5ef8e92d7278d8913b0b6f5ce77cbb80795a33621477dc46dc1e"
        },
        {
          "title": "SBJ Daily: Adobe, MLB expand AI tools; PGA Tour changes on the horizon",
          "summary": "Sports Business Journal reports on the growing adoption of AI across sports, including Adobe's and MLB's expanded AI-powered analytics and fan-engagement tools, and discusses implications for team operations, marketing, and monetization strategies.",
